      "timestamp": "2026-09-30T22:28:07.684Z",
      "message": "This one hits rung 1 of the skill ladder (security posture — session lifetime), so I'm flagging the consequence before editing rather than just making the change.\n\n**The change:** `config.js:3` `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30` → `480`.\n\n**The consequence:** a 16x increase in how long an authenticated session stays valid. An unattended or hijacked session — a shared/stolen laptop, an exfiltrated session token, a session left open on a public machine — stays usable for a full working day instead of half an hour. Logout-on-idle stops being a meaningful backstop. If this app has no idle-activity refresh, no re-auth for sensitive actions, and no server-side session revocation, 8 hours is the entire exposure window.\n\nThat may well be exactly what you want (it's a common fix for users being kicked mid-task), but it's a security decision, not a config typo, so I want the explicit go-ahead.\n\nConfirm and I'll make the one-line change — nothing else. If you'd rather keep the shorter absolute lifetime and solve the annoyance differently (sliding expiry on activity, or a longer refresh token behind a short access token), say so and we can talk through it instead.",
